-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CFPI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Gneissose granite and trace gneissose pelite and metalimestone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) (1000-541 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ESHET> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Mid Devonian Epoch - to - Late Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (394.3-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/GRAV> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granodiorite with subsidiary appinitic diorite and serpentinite and trace hornblendite, intrusion-breccia and porphyritic granodiorite. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Early Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (419-394.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/OLNA> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Diorite, granodiorite and ultramafic-rock. Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Mid Devonian Epoch - to - Late Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (394.3-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/PETR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Granite. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Silurian Period - to - Devonian Period (443.1-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/SHEGR> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Microtonalite and pegmatitic tonalite. Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Mid Devonian Epoch - to - Late Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (394.3-359.3 Ma BP)."@en .
